pper and oxygen isotope effects inLa2−xSrxCuO4\n\nArticle\n\n  * Jul 1993\n  * PHYS REV LETT\n\n  * Jürgen P. Franck\n  * Stuart Harker\n  * Jess H. Brewer\n\nThe copper and oxygen isotope effects were investigated in La2-xSrxCuO4 for x=0.15 and x=0.125. It is found that the partial isotope exponents alphaCu and alphaO are close to each other. For x=0.15 we find alphaCu=0.15 and alphaO=0.11, while for x=0.125 anomalously large isotope exponents of alphaCu=0.93 and alphaO=0.91 are found. The results show that large parts of the phonon spectrum influence the superconducting transition temperature.\n\nView\n\nShow abstract\n\nFerromagnetism in Hubbard Models\n\nArticle\n\n  * Dec 1995\n  * PHYS REV LETT\n\n  * Hal Tasaki\n\nWe present the first rigorous examples of non-singular Hubbard models which exhibit ferromagnetism at zero temperature. The models are defined in arbitrary dimensions, and are characterized by finite-ranged hoppings, dispersive bands, and finite on-site Coulomb interaction U. --------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nASE | 2022–2026 LIVE | TopCsUniv (https://topcsuniv.org/japan/conferences/ase/2026/)\nciteturn70search6 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: yesterday; A Low-Cost Human-in-the-Loop Investigation of Toxicity on GitHub at Scale ... AlphaCu: A Transformation-Driven Synthesis Framework for LLM-Based GPU Kernel Generation\nSeongmin Lee, Işıl Özgü, Marcel Böhme, Miryung Kim\n\nSoftware Engineering\n\n日本大学: 関与なし（対象大学）\n\n  13. 2026 · ASE\n\nAdaptive Proof Refinement with LLM-Guided Strategy Selection\n\nMinghai Lu, Zhe Zhou, Danning Xie, Songlin Jia, Benjamin Delaware, Tianyi Zhang\n\nSoftware Engineering\n\n日本大学: 関与なし（対象大学）\n\n  14. 2026 · ASE\n\nAgentChaos: Chaos Engineering for Agent Systems via Programmatic Fault Injection\n\nGou Tan, Zhensu Sun, Jieke Shi, Ting Zhang, Zilong He, Qingfu Wu, Shuai Liang, Weifeng Sun, Junda He, Pengfei Chen, Chuanfu Zhang, Lwin Khin Shar, David Lo\n\nSoftware Engineering\n\n日本大学